00:07:02,776 --> 00:07:06,807
[Host] Time for a short quiz. Listen and try to answer.

44
00:07:07,408 --> 00:07:13,168
[Slow] 「五山送り火」は、どこで行われましたか。

45
00:07:13,968 --> 00:07:18,815
[Host] In Kyoto — big fires were lit on five mountains around the city.

46
00:07:19,415 --> 00:07:23,759
[Slow] 火は、何時にともりましたか。

47
00:07:24,560 --> 00:07:30,776
[Host] At eight in the evening. The famous character meaning big was lit first, on the eastern mountain.

48
00:07:31,375 --> 00:07:36,271
[Slow] 送り火は、何のための火ですか。

49
00:07:37,072 --> 00:07:44,079
[Host] They are fires for sending off the spirits of ancestors, who people believe come back home in the middle of August.

50
00:07:44,680 --> 00:07:56,920
[Host] That's all for today. Once a year, the mountains of Kyoto light up to say goodbye — to the ancestors, and slowly, to summer itself. See you next time on Japanese Daily News.

51
00:07:57,519 --> 00:07:59,920
[News] また明日。
